<title>USA: Spartan says Q4 loss reflects charge.</title>
<headline>Spartan says Q4 loss reflects charge.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, Mich. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spartan Motors Inc Wednesday on it posted a fourth-quarter loss after taking a one-time charge of $4.4 million related to the closing of its Spartan de Mexico operation.</p>
<p>The company, which makes custom automobile chassis, said it lost $1.2 million, or $0.10 a share, compared with net income of $1.2 million, or $0.10 a share, in the corresponding period a year ago.</p>
<p>Without the charge, net income would have totaled $5.1 million, or $0.41 a share, Spartan said.</p>
<p>The company said revenues fell to $42.4 million from $45.1 million in the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>Its shares closed up 1/8 at 7-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
